Hi Michael,

Ahead of our 2:00 review, Fatima and I have checked the case-split report and=
 the attached condition chart. The January 0.851 is withdrawn: 84 documents f=
rom 24 cases crossed the old partition boundaries, so that evaluation was not=
 independent at the case level.

The new word-frequency linear result is macro-F1 0.832 on 935 evaluation docu=
ments, with the case allocation fixed on April 3. The training-majority basel=
ine is 0.021 on the same documents and labels. The January evaluation had 940=
 documents and a different allocation; the 0.019 difference is not an estimat=
e of the effect of leakage. The 126 Hold documents remain outside allocation =
and scoring.

The report gives the conditions and the reason for withdrawal. I suggest we u=
se the chart to keep the two evaluation sets distinct when we discuss what ca=
n be cited.

Vanessa

